From 026c5669bf8cf8d6c086b3d9556daf1384c8fdc0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Iuri Jikidze <37273763+ijiki16@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 13:17:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 38/39] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: set the TCON-TV endpoint
 index

The display driver takes the TCON index from the DE output endpoint.
Without a reg property the index is 0, the driver selects a TCON top
block that does not exist, and it dereferences a NULL pointer in
tcon_top_hdmi_set_gate(). The vendor device tree uses index 4.

Tested on an OrangePi 4 Pro: the display driver binds without the oops.

Made with the help of an AI coding assistant (Claude).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index e7fb44fce..8655bbfbf 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -574,7 +574,8 @@ disp0: port@0 {
 					reg = <0>;
 					#address-cells = <1>;
 					#size-cells = <0>;
-					disp0_out_tcon3: endpoint {
+					disp0_out_tcon3: endpoint@4 {
+						reg = <4>; /* TCON index read by the driver, as in the vendor DT */
 						remote-endpoint = <&tcon3_in_disp0>;
 					};
 				};
